WEBVTT

00:00:17.661 --> 00:00:18.704
Harry.

00:00:34.136 --> 00:00:36.305
Bring it over here. Over here.

00:00:37.222 --> 00:00:39.308
Oh, go on, Seamus. Go on, get it.

00:00:55.741 --> 00:00:57.159
Good morning, children.

00:00:59.161 --> 00:01:04.333
Ordinary Wizarding Level examinations.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.086
O-W-Ls.

00:01:07.252 --> 00:01:10.580
More commonly known as OWLs.

00:01:12.007 --> 00:01:14.835
Study hard and you will be rewarded.

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:19.744
Fail to do so,
and the consequences may be severe.

00:01:26.313 --> 00:01:30.640
Your previous instruction in this subject
has been disturbingly uneven.

00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:33.696
But you'll be pleased to know,
from now on...

00:01:33.862 --> 00:01:37.366
...you will be following a carefully
structured, Ministry-approved...

00:01:37.533 --> 00:01:39.842
...course of defensive magic. Yes?

00:01:41.537 --> 00:01:44.164
There's nothing in here
about using defensive spells?

00:01:44.331 --> 00:01:45.874
Using spells? Ha-ha!

00:01:46.041 --> 00:01:49.503
Well, I can't imagine why you would
need to use spells in my classroom.

00:01:50.963 --> 00:01:52.798
We're not gonna use magic?

00:01:52.965 --> 00:01:57.310
You'll be learning about defensive spells
in a secure, risk-free way.

00:01:58.137 --> 00:02:00.889
What use is that?
If we're attacked, it won't be risk-free.

00:02:01.056 --> 00:02:03.538
Students will raise their
hands when they speak in my class.

00:02:07.646 --> 00:02:09.625
It is the view of the Ministry...

00:02:10.232 --> 00:02:12.985
...that a theoretical knowledge
will be sufficient...

00:02:13.152 --> 00:02:15.112
...to get you through your examinations...

00:02:15.279 --> 00:02:17.340
...which, after all,
is what school is all about.

00:02:17.906 --> 00:02:20.701
And how's theory supposed to prepare us
for what's out there?

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.911
There is nothing out there, dear.

00:02:23.078 --> 00:02:26.081
Who do you imagine
wants to attack children like yourself?

00:02:26.248 --> 00:02:29.083
Oh, I don't know. Maybe Lord Voldemort.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.405
Now, let me make this quite plain.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.397
You have been told...

00:02:46.894 --> 00:02:51.714
...that a certain dark wizard
is at large once again.

00:02:52.441 --> 00:02:57.571
-This is a lie.
-It's not a lie. I saw him. I fought him.

00:02:57.618 --> 00:02:59.364
Detention, Mr. Potter.

00:02:59.531 --> 00:03:01.700
Cedric Diggory dropped dead
of his own accord?

00:03:01.867 --> 00:03:04.286
Cedric Diggory's death
was a tragic accident.

00:03:04.453 --> 00:03:06.442
It was murder. Voldemort killed him.

00:03:06.529 --> 00:03:07.800
Enough!

00:03:08.957 --> 00:03:10.626
Enough.

00:03:10.793 --> 00:03:14.031
See me later, Mr. Potter. My office.

00:03:39.863 --> 00:03:41.073
Come in.

00:03:46.328 --> 00:03:47.687
Good evening, Mr. Potter.

00:03:48.872 --> 00:03:50.165
Sit.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.380
You're going to be doing some lines
for me today, Mr. Potter.

00:04:01.927 --> 00:04:03.314
No, not with your quill.

00:04:04.012 --> 00:04:06.054
Going to be using
a rather special one of mine.

00:04:12.354 --> 00:04:13.772
Now...

00:04:14.731 --> 00:04:19.952
...I want you to write,
"I must not tell lies."

00:04:22.698 --> 00:04:24.155
How many times?

00:04:25.113 --> 00:04:29.705
Well, let's say for as long as it takes
for the message to sink in.

00:04:31.707 --> 00:04:32.955
You haven't given me any ink.

00:04:33.542 --> 00:04:34.863
Oh, you won't need any ink.

